    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-d772ca6c69c4\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"gcs-wrong-siphash-rounds-xs\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"(?:[Gg][Cc][Ss]|[Bb][Ii][Pp][-_ ]?158|[Bb]lock_?[Ff]ilter|BLOCK_FILTER|[Cc]ompact_?[Ff]ilter|COMPACT_FILTER).*(?:[Ss]ip|SIP)_?(?:[Hh]ash|HASH)(?:er|ER)?[-_]?(?:[013-9][-_]?[0-9]|2[-_]?[0-35-9])\\\\b|(?:[Ss]ip|SIP)_?(?:[Hh]ash|HASH)(?:er|ER)?[-_]?(?:[013-9][-_]?[0-9]|2[-_]?[0-35-9])\\\\b.*(?:[Gg][Cc][Ss]|[Bb][Ii][Pp][-_ ]?158|[Bb]lock_?[Ff]ilter|BLOCK_FILTER|[Cc]ompact_?[Ff]ilter|COMPACT_FILTER)\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.?s\"},{\"id\":\"gcs-wrong-siphash-rounds-py\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"(?:[Gg][Cc][Ss]|[Bb][Ii][Pp][-_ ]?158|[Bb]lock_?[Ff]ilter|BLOCK_FILTER|[Cc]ompact_?[Ff]ilter|COMPACT_FILTER).*(?:[Ss]ip|SIP)_?(?:[Hh]ash|HASH)(?:er|ER)?[-_]?(?:[013-9][-_]?[0-9]|2[-_]?[0-35-9])\\\\b|(?:[Ss]ip|SIP)_?(?:[Hh]ash|HASH)(?:er|ER)?[-_]?(?:[013-9][-_]?[0-9]|2[-_]?[0-35-9])\\\\b.*(?:[Gg][Cc][Ss]|[Bb][Ii][Pp][-_ ]?158|[Bb]lock_?[Ff]ilter|BLOCK_FILTER|[Cc]ompact_?[Ff]ilter|COMPACT_FILTER)\",\"path\":\".floor/added/**/*.py\"}],\"coverage\":\"The flagrant literal case in added .ts/.js/.rs/.cs (and .tsx/.jsx via the ?s glob only for 2-letter extensions) and .py lines: one line that names a block-filter context (GCS, BIP158, block/compact filter) together with a SipHash variant whose round numbers are explicitly not 2-4 (e.g. siphash13, SipHash_1_3, SipHasher48).\",\"residual\":\"Does this hunk hash items for a BIP-158 block filter with SipHash rounds other than 2-4, with a key other than the first 16 bytes of the block hash in its little-endian form, or with a byte-reversed block hash, in a way not captured by an explicit wrong-rounds SipHash name on a line that also names the filter?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/filter/gcs.ts b/src/filter/gcs.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/filter/gcs.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\\n+const h = siphash13(key, item); // BIP158 GCS item hash\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/filters/gcs.py b/filters/gcs.py\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/filters/gcs.py\\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\\n+gcs_hash = siphash.SipHash_1_3(key).hash(item)\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"diff --git a/src/filter/gcs.ts b/src/filter/gcs.ts\\nnew file mode 100644\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/filter/gcs.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\\n+const h = siphash24(key, item); // BIP158 GCS item hash\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"An explicit non-2-4 SipHash variant named on the same line as a block-filter term is a literal violation. Other cases need judgement: whether the hunk builds a block filter at all, the key derivation, and byte order. A reversal can be the correct conversion from display hex to little-endian. Rounds set by parameters, or spread over several lines, also need judgement. So the class is partial.\"}",
